'' B-compat-1 / TB-002, RUN: '{ ( "a" ), ( "b" ) }' over an array of a UDT with a string or
'' ustring field segfaulted. fbc-modern 1.20 refuses the declaration (error 24); tiko supports
'' it (author's decision), so the expected output is fbc-modern's for the same program with the
'' fields declared 'zstring * 8'.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/init-udt-array-paren-str.tiko -o tests/codegen/initudtparenstr.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/initudtparenstr.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ab
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 [one] 1.5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  2 [two] 2.5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  0 [] 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: seveneight 8 s0s1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: seveneight 8 s0+s1
